{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The outdoor waterproof duct tape felt useful for small outdoor repairs alongside my recent outdoor deck screws, so I would try it.",
    "The repair and fastening supplies reflected part of my recent activity, though only the outdoor tape matched something I would choose now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Hose clamps, hose fittings, and battery connectors require specific jobs and dimensions that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Finish nails are not interchangeable with framing nails; their purpose and nailer requirements matter more to me than both being nails.",
    "Locking nuts, cutting wheels, hook-and-loop strips, and epoxy address tasks I do not currently have, even though they can all be used for repairs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying construction supplies seemed to be treated as a reason to recommend almost any workshop or repair supply.",
    "My framing nail purchases seemed to suggest a need for other nails and pneumatic accessories without enough attention to their specific uses or compatibility."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of framing nails, wood screws, and drywall anchors point toward construction and secure mounting tasks.",
    "Fastener dimensions, intended material, and tool compatibility affect whether a similar-looking item is actually useful to me.",
    "My vacuum bags and medicine cups served separate needs; they do not make unrelated maintenance supplies useful to me right now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my repair activity but stretched it beyond my current construction and mounting needs."
}"}
